        ],
        "description": "The video opens on a frame-high blinking caret that types 'N', flashes 'No', then pulls back to a normal-size 'Notion is...' whose dots keep running while the voice-over hesitates.",
        "why_premium": "Turns the product's own core interaction (typing in a blank page) into the hook with nothing but type and scale, which shows confidence and restraint and sets up a question the film pays off."
      },
      {
        "shots": [
          "s004"
        ],
        "description": "A 67 s single continuous take where scenes (negation lines, workspace, AI prompt, transcript, kanban, search, chat, logo wall, roadmap) hand off through camera pushes and morphs with no cuts, guided by a persistent line-drawn mascot.",
        "why_premium": "Cut-free choreography of 36 timed events in one shared space reads as one coherent product, not a montage of screenshots, and needs careful timeline engineering that cheap explainers skip."
      },
      {
        "shots": [
          "s005"
        ],
        "description": "Bookend: 'Notion is...' is retyped, deleted back to 'Notion' and rewritten as 'Notion does', while a checklist of busywork ticks itself off and ends on one empty 'To-do' with the cursor resting on it before the logo lockup.",
        "why_premium": "The edit-in-place answer to its own opening question gives the script a clear payoff, and leaving the last to-do unticked visually lands 'so you can do your life's work' without extra copy."
      }
    ],
